INSERT INTO "techfix_solution" VALUES(218,'Screen flickering — Lenovo LOQ 15 (2025)','[Lenovo Lenovo LOQ 15 (2025)] Display flickers, flashes, or shows lines.','Step 1: Update display and GPU drivers. Step 2: Test with an external monitor to isolate panel vs GPU. Step 3: Change refresh rate to the panel default (60/120/144Hz). Step 4: Check the display cable if flicker changes with lid angle. Step 5: Replace panel/cable at service if hardware-side.','Medium','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MsLtrhwd8Pk','2026-10-16 05:32:55.991429','2026-10-16 05:32:55.991429',4,216);
INSERT INTO "techfix_solution" VALUES(219,'Some keyboard keys not working — Lenovo Yoga Slim 7x Snapdragon','[Lenovo Lenovo Yoga Slim 7x Snapdragon] Certain keys type nothing or repeat characters.','Step 1: Blow out debris with compressed air, shake gently upside down. Step 2: Test with an external keyboard. Step 3: Update/reinstall keyboard driver. Step 4: Check for sticky-keys or filter-keys settings. Step 5: Replace keyboard module if a row/column is dead.','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xOPYH9xve_8','2026-10-16 05:32:56.094576','2026-10-16 05:32:56.094576',4,217);
INSERT INTO "techfix_solution" VALUES(220,'No sound from speakers — Lenovo Yoga Slim 7x Snapdragon','[Lenovo Lenovo Yoga Slim 7x Snapdragon] Videos play but no audio from built-in speakers.','Step 1: Check volume mixer and that the right output is selected. Step 2: Unplug HDMI/Bluetooth devices that may hijack audio. Step 3: Reinstall audio driver from maker site. Step 4: Run the built-in audio troubleshooter. Step 5: Test with earphones to isolate speaker hardware.','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bNOtWInFQOk','2026-10-16 05:32:56.102806','2026-10-16 05:32:56.102806',4,217);
INSERT INTO "techfix_solution" VALUES(221,'Blue screen / random crashes — Lenovo Yoga 9i 14 Gen 9','[Lenovo Lenovo Yoga 9i 14 Gen 9] BSOD errors or sudden restarts under load.','Step 1: Note the stop code and failing driver file. Step 2: Update GPU/chipset drivers and Windows. Step 3: Run memory test (mdsched) and disk check (chkdsk). Step 4: Stress-test thermals; overheating causes crashes. Step 5: Back up data and reinstall OS; service board/RAM if it persists.','Hard','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Fwv_lTLGQ5U','2026-10-16 05:32:56.207543','2026-10-16 05:32:56.207543',4,218);
INSERT INTO "techfix_solution" VALUES(222,'Touchpad not responding — Lenovo Yoga 9i 14 Gen 9','[Lenovo Lenovo Yoga 9i 14 Gen 9] Cursor frozen or touchpad gestures dead.','Step 1: Press the touchpad toggle key (Fn+F-key). Step 2: Check Settings > Bluetooth & devices > Touchpad is enabled. Step 3: Reinstall precision touchpad driver. Step 4: Test in BIOS to rule out software. Step 5: Reseat/replace the touchpad ribbon cable at service.','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UsPEK6uyyrU','2026-10-16 05:32:56.219790','2026-10-16 05:32:56.219790',4,218);
INSERT INTO "techfix_solution" VALUES(223,'Laptop won''t turn on — Lenovo ThinkPad X1 Carbon Gen 13','[Lenovo Lenovo ThinkPad X1 Carbon Gen 13] Pressing power does nothing; no lights or fan spin.','Step 1: Hold power 15s to force-drain. Step 2: Unplug all USB devices and charger. Step 3: Plug the original charger, wait 10 mins, try again. Step 4: Reseat battery if removable. Step 5: Try a known-good charger. Step 6: Bring to service if still dead (possible board issue).','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=a7XAJAyRndA','2026-10-16 05:32:56.315711','2026-10-16 05:32:56.315711',4,219);
INSERT INTO "techfix_solution" VALUES(224,'Battery drains too fast — Lenovo ThinkPad X1 Carbon Gen 13','[Lenovo Lenovo ThinkPad X1 Carbon Gen 13] Battery drops quickly even on light use.','Step 1: Lower brightness to 50% and enable Battery Saver. Step 2: Check battery usage in Settings, close background hogs. Step 3: Update BIOS and drivers. Step 4: Generate battery report (powercfg /batteryreport) and check wear. Step 5: Replace battery if wear exceeds 30%.','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lpMGVM8lPTU','2026-10-16 05:32:56.323972','2026-10-16 05:32:56.323972',4,219);
INSERT INTO "techfix_solution" VALUES(225,'Laptop overheats / fan very loud — Lenovo ThinkPad T14 Gen 5','[Lenovo Lenovo ThinkPad T14 Gen 5] Hot chassis, loud fans, sudden slowdowns or shutdowns.','Step 1: Use on a hard flat surface (not bed/pillow). Step 2: Clean vents with compressed air. Step 3: Check Task Manager for runaway processes. Step 4: Use a cooling pad. Step 5: Re-paste CPU/GPU and replace thermal pads if temps stay above 95C (service center).','Medium','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Xw-5AVnLir8','2026-10-16 05:32:56.436705','2026-10-16 05:32:56.436705',4,220);
INSERT INTO "techfix_solution" VALUES(226,'WiFi keeps disconnecting — Lenovo ThinkPad T14 Gen 5','[Lenovo Lenovo ThinkPad T14 Gen 5] WiFi drops randomly while other devices stay connected.','Step 1: Forget the network and reconnect. Step 2: Update the WiFi driver from the maker site. Step 3: In Device Manager, disable ''allow computer to turn off this device'' for the WiFi adapter. Step 4: Switch between 2.4GHz and 5GHz bands. Step 5: Reset network stack (netsh winsock reset).','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vH6qlgXS2H4','2026-10-16 05:32:56.444548','2026-10-16 05:32:56.444548',4,220);
