INSERT INTO "techfix_solution" VALUES(302,'Touchpad not responding — Microsoft Surface Laptop 7 13.8 Copilot+','[Microsoft Microsoft Surface Laptop 7 13.8 Copilot+] Cursor frozen or touchpad gestures dead.','Step 1: Press the touchpad toggle key (Fn+F-key). Step 2: Check Settings > Bluetooth & devices > Touchpad is enabled. Step 3: Reinstall precision touchpad driver. Step 4: Test in BIOS to rule out software. Step 5: Reseat/replace the touchpad ribbon cable at service.','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5u-EnPphWHs','2026-10-16 05:33:00.685972','2026-10-16 05:33:00.685972',4,407);
INSERT INTO "techfix_solution" VALUES(303,'Laptop won''t turn on — Microsoft Surface Pro 11 Copilot+','[Microsoft Microsoft Surface Pro 11 Copilot+] Pressing power does nothing; no lights or fan spin.','Step 1: Hold power 15s to force-drain. Step 2: Unplug all USB devices and charger. Step 3: Plug the original charger, wait 10 mins, try again. Step 4: Reseat battery if removable. Step 5: Try a known-good charger. Step 6: Bring to service if still dead (possible board issue).','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tLpDCVVfbRc','2026-10-16 05:33:00.781927','2026-10-16 05:33:00.781927',4,408);
INSERT INTO "techfix_solution" VALUES(304,'Battery drains too fast — Microsoft Surface Pro 11 Copilot+','[Microsoft Microsoft Surface Pro 11 Copilot+] Battery drops quickly even on light use.','Step 1: Lower brightness to 50% and enable Battery Saver. Step 2: Check battery usage in Settings, close background hogs. Step 3: Update BIOS and drivers. Step 4: Generate battery report (powercfg /batteryreport) and check wear. Step 5: Replace battery if wear exceeds 30%.','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_LQmFOt0C7I','2026-10-16 05:33:00.794534','2026-10-16 05:33:00.794534',4,408);
INSERT INTO "techfix_solution" VALUES(305,'Laptop overheats / fan very loud — Huawei MateBook D 15 (2024)','[Huawei Huawei MateBook D 15 (2024)] Hot chassis, loud fans, sudden slowdowns or shutdowns.','Step 1: Use on a hard flat surface (not bed/pillow). Step 2: Clean vents with compressed air. Step 3: Check Task Manager for runaway processes. Step 4: Use a cooling pad. Step 5: Re-paste CPU/GPU and replace thermal pads if temps stay above 95C (service center).','Medium','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WeAz-ScJxSM','2026-10-16 05:33:00.893416','2026-10-16 05:33:00.893416',4,409);
INSERT INTO "techfix_solution" VALUES(306,'WiFi keeps disconnecting — Huawei MateBook D 15 (2024)','[Huawei Huawei MateBook D 15 (2024)] WiFi drops randomly while other devices stay connected.','Step 1: Forget the network and reconnect. Step 2: Update the WiFi driver from the maker site. Step 3: In Device Manager, disable ''allow computer to turn off this device'' for the WiFi adapter. Step 4: Switch between 2.4GHz and 5GHz bands. Step 5: Reset network stack (netsh winsock reset).','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=E6eT-RYTVj4','2026-10-16 05:33:00.903345','2026-10-16 05:33:00.903345',4,409);
INSERT INTO "techfix_solution" VALUES(307,'Very slow boot / Windows sluggish — Huawei MateBook X Pro (2024)','[Huawei Huawei MateBook X Pro (2024)] Takes minutes to boot; apps lag and freeze.','Step 1: Disable unnecessary Startup apps in Task Manager. Step 2: Free disk space (min 15% free). Step 3: Run antivirus/malware scan. Step 4: Upgrade to SSD and add RAM if still on HDD/4GB. Step 5: Reinstall Windows as a last resort after backup.','Medium','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CcFY5GTdbIk','2026-10-16 05:33:00.995607','2026-10-16 05:33:00.995607',4,410);
INSERT INTO "techfix_solution" VALUES(308,'Screen flickering — Huawei MateBook X Pro (2024)','[Huawei Huawei MateBook X Pro (2024)] Display flickers, flashes, or shows lines.','Step 1: Update display and GPU drivers. Step 2: Test with an external monitor to isolate panel vs GPU. Step 3: Change refresh rate to the panel default (60/120/144Hz). Step 4: Check the display cable if flicker changes with lid angle. Step 5: Replace panel/cable at service if hardware-side.','Medium','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qm5hYltVWFo','2026-10-16 05:33:01.003759','2026-10-16 05:33:01.003759',4,410);
INSERT INTO "techfix_solution" VALUES(309,'Some keyboard keys not working — LG Gram 16 (2024)','[LG LG Gram 16 (2024)] Certain keys type nothing or repeat characters.','Step 1: Blow out debris with compressed air, shake gently upside down. Step 2: Test with an external keyboard. Step 3: Update/reinstall keyboard driver. Step 4: Check for sticky-keys or filter-keys settings. Step 5: Replace keyboard module if a row/column is dead.','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=88QKDRB_kY4','2026-10-16 05:33:01.098532','2026-10-16 05:33:01.098851',4,411);
INSERT INTO "techfix_solution" VALUES(310,'No sound from speakers — LG Gram 16 (2024)','[LG LG Gram 16 (2024)] Videos play but no audio from built-in speakers.','Step 1: Check volume mixer and that the right output is selected. Step 2: Unplug HDMI/Bluetooth devices that may hijack audio. Step 3: Reinstall audio driver from maker site. Step 4: Run the built-in audio troubleshooter. Step 5: Test with earphones to isolate speaker hardware.','Easy','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HXGiSv75yis','2026-10-16 05:33:01.111114','2026-10-16 05:33:01.111114',4,411);
